      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "At this scale, moving condensate is no longer a matter of pressure or pipe capacity. Every connected conduit becomes part of the same quantum network, allowing its contents to be observed and extracted from anywhere. What you need is a way to impose direction upon something that does not particularly care which way it travels.\n\nLike the theoretical demon whose name it bears, the §5§lMaxwell Gate§r separates one state from another. Networks connected to its output may observe and pull condensate from the input, while the input remains blind to everything beyond the gate. A filter in the controller can further restrict this passage to a single type of condensate.\n\nThere is one exception: the Entanglement Apparatus sees the gate backwards. It may only push condensate from the output network toward the input network.\n\n[note]The Maxwell Gate is optional. It does not move condensate by itself; it only controls which side may access it.[/note]\n\n[note]The Gate consumes a constant 1A of UIV power whenever active, even when no condensate is passing through it.[/note]",
